{"argv":["bash","-lc","cat > AUTHORIZATION.md <<EOF\n# Authorization review\n\nA signed-in user can obtain another tenant\u2019s case record through `caseById`. The function receives the signed-in actor, but never reads or validates `actor.tenantId`. Instead, the SQL query filters by `request.tenantId` and `request.id`, both supplied by the caller. For example, an actor from `north` can request `{ tenantId: \"south\", id: 2 }` and receive the South record.\n\nThe relevant cause is the missing authorization check tying the query\u2019s tenant filter to the authenticated actor; tenant scoping is controlled by request input rather than the actor identity.\nEOF\nnpm test\nnpm run check"],"cwd":"/tmp/repository-agent-study/r05","event":"command_started","max_commands":30,"output_cap_bytes":24000,"recorded_at_ns":1788738951429106147,"sequence":2,"timeout_seconds":120.0}
